  "title": "Aamal & Dua of Umm Dawood",
  "data": "Fast on the 13th, 14th and 15th of Rajab.\nAt midday on the 15th, perform ghusl.\nAfter midday, offer the Zuhr and Asr prayers with full care, in a quiet place where nothing will distract you and no one will speak to you.\nAfter the prayers, facing the qiblah, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) 100 times, [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) 100 times and [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) 10 times.\nThen recite [Surah al-An'am](A10), [Surah al-Isra](A21), [Surah al-Kahf](A22), [Surah Luqman](A35), [Surah Yasin](A40), [Surah al-Saffat](A41), [Surah al-Zukhruf](A47), [Surah al-Shura](A46), [Surah al-Dukhan](A48), [Surah al-Fath](A52), [Surah al-Waqi'ah](A60), [Surah al-Mulk](A71), [Surah al-Qalam](A72), and [Surah al-Inshiqaq](A88) with every surah after it to the end of the Qur'an.\nStill facing the qiblah, recite this dua:\nصَدَقَ اللّٰهُ الْعَظِيْمُ\nSADAQALLAAHUL A'ZEEM\nTrue are the words of Allah, the All-great.\nالَّذِيْ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ الْحَيُّ الْقَيُّوْمُ ذُو الْجَلَالِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ\nALLADHEE LAA ILAAHA ILLAA HUWAL HAYYUL QAYYOOMU DHUL JALAALI WAL IKRAAM\nThere is no god save Him, the Ever-living, the Eternal, The Lord of Majesty and Honor,\nالرَّحْمٰنُ الرَّحِيْمُ الْحَلِيْمُ الْكَرِيْمُ\nAR-RAHMAANUR RAHEEMUL HALEEMUL KAREEM\nthe All-beneficent, the All-merciful, the Forbearing, the All-generous.\nالَّذِيْ لَيْسَ كَمِثْلِهٖ شَيْ‏ءٌ وَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ الْبَصِيْرُ الْخَبِيْرُ\nALLADHEE LAYSA KAMITHLIHEE SHAY'UN WA HUWAS SAMEE'UL A'LEEMUL BASEERUL KHABEER\nThere is nothing like Him, and He is the All-hearing, the All-knowing, the All-seeing, the All-aware.\nشَهِدَ اللّٰهُ اَنَّهٗ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ وَالْمَلَاۤئِكَةُ وَاُوْلُوا الْعِلْمِ قَاۤئِمًا بِالْقِسْطِ\nSHAHIDALLAAHU ANNAHOO LAA ILAAHA ILLAA HUWA WAL MALAA'IKATU WA OOLUL I'LMI QAA'IMAN BIL QIST\nAllah bears witness that there is no god but He, and (so do) the angels and those possessed of knowledge, maintaining His creation with justice.\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA HUWAL A'ZEEZUL HAKEEM\nThere is no god but He, the Mighty, the Wise.\nوَبَلَّغَتْ رُسُلُهُ الْكِرَامُ\nWA BALLAGHAT RUSULUHUL KIRAAM\nHis noble Messengers have conveyed the mission\nوَاَنَا عَلٰى ذٰلِكَ مِنَ الشَّاهِدِيْنَ\nWA ANAA A'LAA DHAALIKA MINASH SHAAHIDEEN\nand I am of those who bear witness to that.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَكَ الْحَمْدُ وَلَكَ الْمَجْدُ وَلَكَ الْعِزُّ وَلَكَ الْفَخْرُ\nALLAAHUMMA LAKAL HAMDU WA LAKAL MAJDU WA LAKAL I'ZZU WA LAKAL FAKHR\nO Allah, to You belongs praise, to You belongs glory, to You belongs might, to You belongs pride,\nوَلَكَ الْقَهْرُ وَلَكَ النِّعْمَةُ وَلَكَ الْعَظَمَةُ وَلَكَ الرَّحْمَةُ\nWA LAKAL QAHRU WA LAKAN NI'MATU WA LAKAL A'ZAMATU WA LAKAR RAHMAH\nto You belongs supreme power, to You belong bounties, to You belongs greatness, to You belongs mercy,\nوَلَكَ الْمَهَابَةُ وَلَكَ السُّلْطَانُ وَلَكَ الْبَهَاءُ وَلَكَ الْاِمْتِنَانُ\nWA LAKAL MAHAABATU WA LAKAS SULTAANU WA LAKAL BAHAA'U WA LAKAL IMTINAAN\nto You belongs reverence, to You belongs sovereignty, to You belongs beauty, to You belongs benevolence,\nوَلَكَ التَّسْبِيْحُ وَلَكَ التَّقْدِيْسُ وَلَكَ التَّهْلِيْلُ وَلَكَ التَّكْبِيْرُ\nWA LAKAT TASBEEHU WA LAKAT TAQDEESU WA LAKAT TAHLEELU WA LAKAT TAKBEER\nto You belongs glorification, to You belongs holiness, to You belongs the confession of Your being the One and Only God, to You belongs the confession of Your being the most Great Lord,\nوَلَكَ مَا يُرَىٰ وَلَكَ مَا لَا يُرَىٰ\nWA LAKA MAA YURAA WA LAKA MAA LAA YURAA\nto You belongs that which is seen, to You belongs that which is not seen,\nوَلَكَ مَا فَوْقَ السَّمَاوَاتِ الْعُلَىٰ\nWA LAKA MAA FAWQAS SAMAAWAATIL U'LAA\nto You belongs that which is far above the high heavens,\nوَلَكَ مَا تَحْتَ الثَّرَىٰ\nWA LAKA MAA TAHTATH THARAA\nto You belongs that which is deep down under the abyss,\nوَلَكَ الْاَرَضُوْنَ السُّفْلٰى\nWA LAKAL ARADOONAS SUFLAA\nto You belong the worlds below the heavens,\nوَلَكَ الْاٰخِرَةُ وَالْاُوْلٰى\nWA LAKAL AAKHIRATU WAL OOLAA\nto You belong the end and the beginning,\nوَلَكَ مَا تَرْضَىٰ بِهٖ مِنَ الثَّنَاءِ وَالْحَمْدِ وَالشُّكْرِ وَالنَّعْمَاءِ\nWA LAKA MAA TARDAA BIHEE MINATH THANAA'I WAL HAMDI WASH SHUKRI WAN NA'MAA'\nand to You is all thanks, all praise, all gratitude, and all bliss as much as it pleases You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى جَبْرَئِيْلَ اَمِيْنِكَ عَلٰى وَحْيِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA JABRA'EELA AMEENIKA A'LAA WAHYIK\nO Allah, (please do) send blessings to (Archangel) Gabriel, the trustee on Your revelations,\nوَالْقَوِيِّ عَلٰى اَمْرِكَ وَالْمُطَاعِ فِي سَمَاوَاتِكَ وَمَحَالِّ كَرَامَاتِكَ\nWAL QAWIYYI A'LAA AMRIKA WAL MUTAA'I FEE SAMAAWAATIKA WA MAHAALLI KARAAMAATIK\nthe firm in conveying Your orders, the obeyed in Your heavens and the places where Your honoring lies,\nالْمُتَحَمِّلِ لِكَلِمَاتِكَ النَّاصِرِ لِاَنْبِيَاۤئِكَ الْمُدَمِّرِ لِاَعْدَاۤئِكَ\nAL-MUTAHAMMILI LIKALIMAATIKAN NAASIRI LI-ANBIYAA'IKAL MUDAMMIRI LI-A'DAA'IK\nthe bearer of Your Words, the supporter of Your Prophets, and the terminator of Your enemies.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مِيْكَاۤئِيْلَ مَلَكِ رَحْمَتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MEEKAA'EELA MALAKI RAHMATIK\nO Allah, (please do) send blessings to (Archangel) Michael, the angel of Your mercy,\nوَالْمَخْلُوْقِ لِرَاْفَتِكَ وَالْمُسْتَغْفِرِ الْمُعِيْنِ لِاَهْلِ طَاعَتِكَ\nWAL MAKHLOOQI LIRA'FATIKA WAL MUSTAGHFIRIL MU'EENI LI-AHLI TAA'ATIK\nthe one created for (showing) Your kindness, and the one seeking forgiveness and assisting the people of obedience to You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى اِسْرَافِيْلَ حَامِلِ عَرْشِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA ISRAAFEELA HAAMILI A'RSHIK\nO Allah, (please do) send blessings to Seraph, the bearer of Your Throne,\nوَصَاحِبِ الصُّوْرِ الْمُنْتَظِرِ لِاَمْرِكَ الْوَجِلِ الْمُشْفِقِ مِنْ خِيْفَتِكَ\nWA SAAHIBIS SOORIL MUNTAZIRI LI-AMRIKAL WAJILIL MUSHFIQI MIN KHEEFATIK\nthe one in charge of the Trumpet (that declares the Resurrection Day), the one waiting for Your order, and the one apprehensive and fearful of You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى حَمَلَةِ الْعَرْشِ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA HAMALATIL A'RSHIT TAAHIREEN\nO Allah, (please do) send blessings to the pure angels who bear Your Throne,\nوَعَلَى السَّفَرَةِ الْكِرَامِ الْبَرَرَةِ الطَّيِّبِيْنَ\nWA A'LAS SAFARATIL KIRAAMIL BARARATIT TAYYIBEEN\nupon the scribes; the noble, the virtuous, and the immaculate,\nوَعَلٰى مَلَاۤئِكَتِكَ الْكِرَامِ الْكَاتِبِيْنَ\nWA A'LAA MALAA'IKATIKAL KIRAAMIL KAATIBEEN\nupon Your angels; the virtuous recorders (of the deeds),\nوَعَلٰى مَلَاۤئِكَةِ الْجِنَانِ وَخَزَنَةِ النِّيْرَانِ\nWA A'LAA MALAA'IKATIL JINAANI WA KHAZANATIN NEERAAN\nupon the angels of the gardens of Paradise, upon the keepers of Hellfire,\nوَمَلَكِ الْمَوْتِ وَالْاَعْوَانِ\nWA MALAKIL MAWTI WAL A'WAAN\nand upon the Angel of Death and his assistants.\nيَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ\nYAA DHAL JALAALI WAL IKRAAM\nO Lord of Majesty and Honor!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى اَبِيْنَا اٰدَمَ بَدِيْعِ فِطْرَتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA ABEENAA AADAMA BADEE'I FITRATIK\nO Allah, (please do) send blessings to our father Adam: the foremost of Your creation\nالَّذِيْ كَرَّمْتَهٗ بِسُجُوْدِ مَلَاۤئِكَتِكَ وَاَبَحْتَهٗ جَنَّتَكَ\nALLADHEE KARRAMTAHOO BISUJOODI MALAA'IKATIKA WA ABAHTAHOO JANNATAK\nwhom You honored by making Your angels prostrate themselves before him, and whom You allowed to dwell in Your Paradise.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى اُمِّنَا حَوَّاءَ الْمُطَهَّرَةِ مِنَ الرِّجْسِ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA UMMINAA HAWWAA'AL MUTAHHARATI MINAR RIJS\nO Allah, (please do) send blessings to our mother Eve: the purified from filth,\nالْمُصَفَّاةِ مِنَ الدَّنَسِ الْمُفَضَّلَةِ مِنَ الْاِنْسِ الْمُتَرَدِّدَةِ بَيْنَ مَحَالِّ الْقُدْسِ\nAL-MUSAFFAATI MINAD DANASIL MUFADDALATI MINAL INSIL MUTARADDIDATI BAYNA MAHAALLIL QUDS\nthe cleaned from dirt, the favorite from among the humankind, and the allowed to visit the places of sanctity.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى هَابِيْلَ وَشَيْثٍ وَاِدْرِيْسَ وَنُوْحٍ وَهُوْدٍ وَصَالِحٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA HAABEELA WA SHAYTHIN WA IDREESA WA NOOHIN WA HOODIN WA SAALIH\nO Allah, (please do) send blessings to Abel, Shayth, Idris, Noah, Hud, Salih,\nوَاِبْرَاهِيْمَ وَاِسْمَاعِيْلَ وَاِسْحَاقَ وَيَعْقُوْبَ وَيُوْسُفَ وَالْاَسْبَاطِ\nWA IBRAAHEEMA WA ISMAA'EELA WA IS-HAAQA WA YA'QOOBA WA YOOSUFA WAL ASBAAT\nAbraham, Ishmael, Isaac, Jacob, Joseph, the Tribes,\nوَلُوْطٍ وَشُعَيْبٍ وَاَيُّوْبَ وَمُوْسَىٰ وَهَارُوْنَ وَيُوْشَعَ وَمِيْشَا\nWA LOOTIN WA SHU'AYBIN WA AYYOOBA WA MOOSAA WA HAAROONA WA YOOSHA'A WA MEESHAA\nLot, Shu'ayb, Job, Moses, Aaron, Joshua, Micah,\nوَالْخِضْرِ وَذِي الْقَرْنَيْنِ وَيُوْنُسَ وَاِلْيَاسَ وَالْيَسَعِ وَذِي الْكِفْلِ\nWAL KHIDRI WA DHIL QARNAYNI WA YOONUSA WA ILYAASA WAL YASA'I WA DHIL KIFL\nal-Khidr, Dhu'l-Qarnayn (the two-horned), Jonah, Elias, Elisa, Dhu'l-Kifl,\nوَطَالُوْتَ وَدَاوُدَ وَسُلَيْمَانَ وَزَكَرِيَّا وَشَعْيَا وَيَحْيَىٰ\nWA TAALOOTA WA DAAWUDA WA SULAYMAANA WA ZAKARIYYAA WA SHA'YAA WA YAHYAA\nSaul, David, Solomon, Zachariah, Shayah, John,\nوَتُوْرَخَ وَمَتَّى وَاِرْمِيَا وَحَيْقُوْقَ وَدَانِيَالَ وَعُزَيْرٍ وَعِيْسَىٰ\nWA TOORAKHA WA MATTAA WA IRMIYAA WA HAYQOOQA WA DAANIYAALA WA U'ZAYRIN WA I'EESAA\nTurakh, Matthias, Jeremiah, Habakkuk, Daniel, Ezra, Jesus,\nوَشَمْعُوْنَ وَجِرْجِيْسَ وَالْحَوَارِيِّيْنَ وَالْاَتْبَاعِ وَخَالِدٍ وَحَنْظَلَةَ وَلُقْمَانَ\nWA SHAM'OONA WA JIRJEESA WAL HAWAARIYYEENA WAL ATBAA'I WA KHAALIDIN WA HANZALATA WA LUQMAAN\nSimon, Georges, the Apostles, the Followers, Khalid, Hanzalah, and Luqman.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, (please do) send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَارْحَمْ مُحَمَّدًا وَاٰلَ مُحَمَّدٍ\nWARHAM MUHAMMADAN WA AALA MUHAMMAD\nhave mercy upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَبَارِكْ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nWA BAARIK A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nand send benedictions upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nكَمَا صَلَّيْتَ وَرَحِمْتَ [وَتَرَحَّمْتَ‏] وَبَارَكْتَ عَلٰى اِبْرَاهِيْمَ وَاٰلِ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ\nKAMAA SALLAYTA WA RAHIMTA [WA TARAHHAMTA] WA BAARAKTA A'LAA IBRAAHEEMA WA AALI IBRAAHEEM\njust as You have sent blessings, had mercy, and sent benedictions upon Abraham and the Household of Abraham.\nاِنَّكَ حَمِيْدٌ مَجِيْدٌ\nINNAKA HAMEEDUN MAJEED\nYou are verily worthy of all praise, full of all glory.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى الْاَوْصِيَاءِ وَالسُّعَدَاءِ وَالشُّهَدَاءِ وَاَئِمَّةِ الْهُدَىٰ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAL AWSIYAA'I WAS SU'ADAA'I WASH SHUHADAA'I WA A'IMMATIL HUDAA\nO Allah, (please do) send blessings to the Successors, the happy, the witnesses, and the leaders to the true guidance.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى الْاَبْدَالِ وَالْاَوْتَادِ وَالسُّيَّاحِ وَالْعُبَّادِ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAL ABDAALI WAL AWTAADI WAS SUYYAAHI WAL U'BBAAD\nO Allah, (please do) send blessings to the Substitutes (whom shall be given the favor of participating in Imam al-Mahdi’s campaigns), the loftiest personalities, those observing fasting with devotion, those who ardently serve You,\nوَالْمُخْلِصِيْنَ وَالزُّهَّادِ وَاَهْلِ الْجِدِّ وَالْاِجْتِهَادِ\nWAL MUKHLISEENA WAZ ZUHHAADI WA AHLIL JIDDI WAL IJTIHAAD\nthose whom You have chosen, the ascetic servants, and the people of painstaking and hardworking deeds.\nوَاخْصُصْ مُحَمَّدًا وَاَهْلَ بَيْتِهٖ بِاَفْضَلِ صَلَوَاتِكَ وَاَجْزَلِ كَرَامَاتِكَ\nWAKHSUS MUHAMMADAN WA AHLA BAYTIHEE BI-AFDALI SALAWAATIKA WA AJZALI KARAAMAATIK\n(Please do) give Muhammad and his Household exclusively the best of Your blessings and the most abundant of Your favors.\nوَبَلِّغْ رُوْحَهٗ وَجَسَدَهٗ مِنِّي تَحِيَّةً وَسَلَامًا\nWA BALLIGH ROOHAHOO WA JASADAHOO MINNEE TAHIYYATAN WA SALAAMAA\n(Please do) convey to his soul and body my greetings and compliments\nوَزِدْهُ فَضْلًا وَشَرَفًا وَكَرَمًا\nWA ZID-HU FADLAN WA SHARAFAN WA KARAMAA\nand give him more favors, honor, and esteem\nحَتَّىٰ تُبَلِّغَهٗ اَعْلٰى دَرَجَاتِ اَهْلِ الشَّرَفِ مِنَ النَّبِيِّيْنَ وَالْمُرْسَلِيْنَ وَالْاَفَاضِلِ الْمُقَرَّبِيْنَ\nHATTAA TUBALLIGHAHOO A'LAA DARAJAATI AHLISH SHARAFI MINAN NABIYYEENA WAL MURSALEENA WAL AFAADILIL MUQARRABEEN\nso that You will make him attain the most elevated ranks of the honored ones from amongst the Prophets, the Messengers, and the virtuous, favorable ones.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَصَلِّ عَلٰى مَنْ سَمَّيْتُ وَمَنْ لَمْ اُسَمِّ\nALLAAHUMMA WA SALLI A'LAA MAN SAMMAYTU WA MAN LAM USAMM\nO Allah, (please) send blessings to those whose names I have mentioned or I have not\nمِنْ مَلَاۤئِكَتِكَ وَاَنْبِيَاۤئِكَ وَرُسُلِكَ وَاَهْلِ طَاعَتِكَ\nMIN MALAA'IKATIKA WA ANBIYAA'IKA WA RUSULIKA WA AHLI TAA'ATIK\nfrom amongst Your angels, Prophets, Messengers, and obedient servants.\nوَاَوْصِلْ صَلَوَاتِي اِلَيْهِمْ وَاِلٰى اَرْوَاحِهِمْ\nWA AWSIL SALAWAATEE ILAYHIM WA ILAA ARWAAHIHIM\nConvey my invocations of blessings to them and to their souls\nوَاجْعَلْهُمْ اِخْوَانِي فِيْكَ وَاَعْوَانِي عَلٰى دُعَاۤئِكَ\nWAJ'ALHUM IKHWAANEE FEEKA WA A'WAANEE A'LAA DU'AA'IK\nand make them my brethren in You and make them help me pray You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّي اَسْتَشْفِعُ بِكَ اِلَيْكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE ASTASHFI'U BIKA ILAYK\nO Allah, I seek Your intercession for me to You,\nوَبِكَرَمِكَ اِلٰى كَرَمِكَ\nWA BIKARAMIKA ILAA KARAMIK\nI seek Your honor in the name of Your honor,\nوَبِجُوْدِكَ اِلٰى جُوْدِكَ\nWA BIJOODIKA ILAA JOODIK\nI seek Your magnanimity in the name of Your magnanimity,\nوَبِرَحْمَتِكَ اِلٰى رَحْمَتِكَ، وَبِاَهْلِ طَاعَتِكَ اِلَيْكَ\nWA BIRAHMATIKA ILAA RAHMATIKA WA BI-AHLI TAA'ATIKA ILAYK\nand I seek Your mercy in the name of Your mercy and in the name of the people of the obedience to You.\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ اَللّٰهُمَّ بِكُلِّ مَا سَاَلَكَ بِهٖ اَحَدٌ مِنْهُمْ\nWA AS'ALUKA ALLAAHUMMA BIKULLI MAA SA'ALAKA BIHEE AHADUN MINHUM\nI thus beseech You, O Allah, in the name of all the things by whose names those people have besought You,\nمِنْ مَسْاَلَةٍ شَرِيْفَةٍ غَيْرِ مَرْدُوْدَةٍ\nMIN MAS'ALATIN SHAREEFATIN GHAYRI MARDOODAH\nincluding the honorable requests that are never rejected by You\nوَبِمَا دَعَوْكَ بِهٖ مِنْ دَعْوَةٍ مُجَابَةٍ غَيْرِ مُخَيَّبَةٍ\nWA BIMAA DA'AWKA BIHEE MIN DA'WATIN MUJAABATIN GHAYRI MUKHAYYABAH\nand all the responded and unfailing prayers that they have asked from You.\nيَا اللّٰهُ يَا رَحْمَانُ يَا رَحِيْمُ يَا حَلِيْمُ يَا كَرِيمُ\nYALLAAHU YAA RAHMAANU YAA RAHEEMU YAA HALEEMU YAA KAREEM\nO Allah! O All-beneficent! O All-merciful! O All-forbearing! O All-generous!\nيَا عَظِيْمُ يَا جَلِيْلُ يَا مُنِيْلُ يَا جَمِيْلُ يَا كَفِيْلُ\nYAA A'ZEEMU YAA JALEELU YAA MUNEELU YAA JAMEELU YAA KAFEEL\nO All-great! O All-majestic! O Bestower! O All-munificent! O Surety!\nيَا وَكِيْلُ يَا مُقِيْلُ يَا مُجِيْرُ يَا خَبِيْرُ يَا مُنِيْرُ\nYAA WAKEELU YAA MUQEELU YAA MUJEERU YAA KHABEERU YAA MUNEER\nO Dependable! O Rescuer! O Protector! O All-aware! O All-luminous!\nيَا مُبِيْرُ يَا مَنِيْعُ يَا مُدِيْلُ يَا مُحِيْلُ يَا كَبِيْرُ\nYAA MUBEERU YAA MANEE'U YAA MUDEELU YAA MUHEELU YAA KABEER\nO Eradicator (of the wrongdoers)! O Shielding! O Grantor of victory! O Assuring! O All-big!\nيَا قَدِيْرُ يَا بَصِيْرُ يَا شَكُوْرُ يَا بَرُّ يَا طُهْرُ\nYAA QADEERU YAA BASEERU YAA SHAKOORU YAA BARRU YAA TUHR\nO All-powerful! O All-seer! O most Ready to appreciate (servitude)! O All-benign! O Source of purity!\nيَا طَاهِرُ يَا قَاهِرُ يَا ظَاهِرُ يَا بَاطِنُ يَا سَاتِرُ\nYAA TAAHIRU YAA QAAHIRU YAA ZAAHIRU YAA BAATINU YAA SAATIR\nO All-pure! O Omnipotent! O Evident! O Immanent! O Concealer!\nيَا مُحِيْطُ يَا مُقْتَدِرُ يَا حَفِيْظُ يَا مُتَجَبِّرُ يَا قَرِيْبُ\nYAA MUHEETU YAA MUQTADIRU YAA HAFEEZU YAA MUTAJABBIRU YAA QAREEB\nO All-encompassing! O All-prevailing! O All-guarding! O Invincible! O Nigh!\nيَا وَدُوْدُ يَا حَمِيْدُ يَا مَجِيْدُ يَا مُبْدِئُ يَا مُعِيْدُ\nYAA WADOODU YAA HAMEEDU YAA MAJEEDU YAA MUBDI'U YAA MU'EED\nO Loving! O All-praised! O full of all glory! O Originator! O Reproducer!\nيَا شَهِيْدُ يَا مُحْسِنُ يَا مُجْمِلُ يَا مُنْعِمُ يَا مُفْضِلُ\nYAA SHAHEEDU YAA MUHSINU YAA MUJMILU YAA MUN'IMU YAA MUFDIL\nO Witness! O All-liberal! O All-bountiful! O Source of all bounties! O Doer of favors!\nيَا قَابِضُ يَا بَاسِطُ يَا هَادِيْ يَا مُرْسِلُ يَا مُرْشِدُ\nYAA QAABIDU YAA BAASITU YAA HAADEE YAA MURSILU YAA MURSHID\nO Straitening! O Enlarger! O Guide! O Sender! O Director!\nيَا مُسَدِّدُ يَا مُعْطِي يَا مَانِعُ يَا دَافِعُ يَا رَافِعُ\nYAA MUSADDIDU YAA MU'TEE YAA MAANI'U YAA DAAFI'U YAA RAAFI'\nO Leader (to the truth)! O Giver! O Forbidder! O Repealer! O Raiser!\nيَا بَاقِيْ يَا وَاقِيْ يَا خَلَّاقُ يَا وَهَّابُ يَا تَوَّابُ\nYAA BAAQEE YAA WAAQEE YAA KHALLAAQU YAA WAHHAABU YAA TAWWAAB\nO Eternal! O Guardian! O Creator! O Endower! O Accepter of repentance!\nيَا فَتَّاحُ يَا نَفَّاحُ يَا مُرْتَاحُ يَا مَنْ بِيَدِهٖ كُلُّ مِفْتَاحٍ يَا نَفَّاعُ\nYAA FATTAAHU YAA NAFFAAHU YAA MURTAAHU YAA MAN BIYADIHEE KULLU MIFTAAHIN YAA NAFFAA'\nO Decider! O Donator! O Source of rest! O He Who has in possessions the clues of all things! O Source of profit!\nيَا رَءُوْفُ يَا عَطُوْفُ يَا كَافِيْ يَا شَافِيْ يَا مُعَافِيْ\nYAA RA'OOFU YAA A'TOOFU YAA KAAFEE YAA SHAAFEE YAA MU'AAFEE\nO All-kind! O All-sympathetic! O Securer! O Healer! O Curer!\nيَا مُكَافِيْ يَا وَفِيُّ يَا مُهَيْمِنُ يَا عَزِيْزُ يَا جَبَّارُ\nYAA MUKAAFEE YAA WAFIYYU YAA MUHAYMINU YAA A'ZEEZU YAA JABBAAR\nO Awarder! O Faithful! O Dominant! O Almighty! O All-potent!\nيَا مُتَكَبِّرُ يَا سَلَامُ يَا مُؤْمِنُ يَا اَحَدُ يَا صَمَدُ\nYAA MUTAKABBIRU YAA SALAAMU YAA MU'MINU YAA AHADU YAA SAMAD\nO Superb! O Giver of peace! O Grantor of security! O Only One! O Besought of all!\nيَا نُوْرُ يَا مُدَبِّرُ يَا فَرْدُ يَا وِتْرُ يَا قُدُّوْسُ\nYAA NOORU YAA MUDABBIRU YAA FARDU YAA WITRU YAA QUDDOOS\nO Light! O Manager (of all affairs)! O Single! O Lone! O Holy!\nيَا نَاصِرُ يَا مُوْنِسُ يَا بَاعِثُ يَا وَارِثُ يَا عَالِمُ\nYAA NAASIRU YAA MOONISU YAA BAA'ITHU YAA WAARITHU YAA A'ALIM\nO Giver of victory! O Source of entertainment! O Resurrector! O Inheritor (of all things)! O All-knowing!\nيَا حَاكِمُ يَا بَادِيْ يَا مُتَعَالِي يَا مُصَوِّرُ يَا مُسَلِّمُ\nYAA HAAKIMU YAA BAADEE YAA MUTA'AALEE YAA MUSAWWIRU YAA MUSALLIM\nO Judge! O Originator! O Exalted! O Maker of visions! O Grantor of safety!\nيَا مُتَحَبِّبُ يَا قَاۤئِمُ يَا دَاۤئِمُ يَا عَلِيْمُ يَا حَكِيْمُ\nYAA MUTAHABBIBU YAA QAA'IMU YAA DAA'IMU YAA A'LEEMU YAA HAKEEM\nO Amiable! O Subsistent! O Everlasting! O Knowing! O Wise!\nيَا جَوَادُ يَا بَارِئُ يَا بَارُّ يَا سَارُّ يَا عَدْلُ\nYAA JAWAADU YAA BAARI'U YAA BAARRU YAA SAARRU YAA A'DL\nO All-magnanimous! O Maker! O Caring! O Source of pleasure! O Fair!\nيَا فَاصِلُ يَا دَيَّانُ يَا حَنَّانُ يَا مَنَّانُ يَا سَمِيْعُ\nYAA FAASILU YAA DAYYAANU YAA HANNAANU YAA MANNAANU YAA SAMEE'\nO Distinguishes (between the right and the wrong)! O Master! O All-munificent! O Favorer! O All-hearer!\nيَا بَدِيْعُ يَا خَفِيْرُ يَا مُعِينُ [مُغَيِّرُ] يَا نَاشِرُ يَا غَافِرُ\nYAA BADEE'U YAA KHAFEERU YAA MU'EENU [MUGHAYYIRU] YAA NAASHIRU YAA GHAAFIR\nO best Maker! O Observer! O Helper! O Extender (of mercy)! O Forgiver!\nيَا قَدِيْمُ يَا مُسَهِّلُ يَا مُيَسِّرُ يَا مُمِيْتُ يَا مُحْيِيْ\nYAA QADEEMU YAA MUSAHHILU YAA MUYASSIRU YAA MUMEETU YAA MUHYEE\nO Eternal! O Alleviator! O Reliever! O He Who causes to die! O Grantor of life!\nيَا نَافِعُ يَا رَازِقُ يَا مُقْتَدِرُ [مُقَدِّرُ] يَا مُسَبِّبُ يَا مُغِيْثُ\nYAA NAAFI'U YAA RAAZIQU YAA MUQTADIRU [MUQADDIRU] YAA MUSABBIBU YAA MUGHEETH\nO Grantor of benefits! O Provider of sustenance! O All-competent! O Creator of causes! O Aide!\nيَا مُغْنِيْ يَا مُقْنِيْ يَا خَالِقُ يَا رَاصِدُ يَا وَاحِدُ\nYAA MUGHNEE YAA MUQNEE YAA KHAALIQU YAA RAASIDU YAA WAAHID\nO Grantor of wealth! O Giver to hold! O Creator! O Onlooker! O One!\nيَا حَاضِرُ يَا جَابِرُ يَا حَافِظُ يَا شَدِيْدُ يَا غِيَاثُ\nYAA HAADIRU YAA JAABIRU YAA HAAFIZU YAA SHADEEDU YAA GHIYAATH\nO Present! O Mender! O Safeguarding! O Firm (in punishment)! O Aid!\nيَا عَاۤئِدُ يَا قَابِضُ\nYAA A'A'IDU YAA QAABID\nO Donor! O Straitening!\nيَا مَنْ عَلَا فَاسْتَعْلٰى فَكَانَ بِالْمَنْظَرِ الْاَعْلٰى\nYAA MAN A'LAA FASTA'LAA FAKAANA BIL MANZARIL A'LAA\nO He Who has mounted to the most elevated point, He thus occupies the most exalted site!\nيَا مَنْ قَرُبَ فَدَنَا وَبَعُدَ فَنَاَىٰ وَعَلِمَ السِّرَّ وَاَخْفَى\nYAA MAN QARUBA FADANAA WA BA'UDA FANA'AA WA A'LIMAS SIRRA WA AKHFAA\nO He Who has approached so closely that He has become the nearest of all things and, at the same time, He has been so far that He is in the furthest point, and He has known the secret and even what is more hidden!\nيَا مَنْ اِلَيْهِ التَّدْبِيْرُ وَلَهُ الْمَقَادِيْرُ\nYAA MAN ILAYHIT TADBEERU WA LAHUL MAQAADEER\nO He to Whom all management is relegated and to Whom all measures are referred!\nوَيَا مَنِ الْعَسِيْرُ عَلَيْهِ سَهْلٌ يَسِيْرٌ\nWA YAA MANIL A'SEERU A'LAYHI SAHLUN YASEER\nO He for Whom the most difficult thing is easy and simple!\nيَا مَنْ هُوَ عَلٰى مَا يَشَاءُ قَدِيْرٌ\nYAA MAN HUWA A'LAA MAA YASHAA'U QADEER\nO He Who has power to do whatever He wills!\nيَا مُرْسِلَ الرِّيَاحِ يَا فَالِقَ الْاِصْبَاحِ\nYAA MURSILAR RIYAAHI YAA FAALIQAL ISBAAH\nO He Who sends forth the wind! O He Who causes the dawn to break!\nيَا بَاعِثَ الْاَرْوَاحِ يَا ذَا الْجُوْدِ وَالسَّمَاحِ\nYAA BAA'ITHAL ARWAAHI YAA DHAL JOODI WAS SAMAAH\nO He Who revives the spirits! O Lord of magnanimity and lenience!\nيَا رَادَّ مَا قَدْ فَاتَ يَا نَاشِرَ الْاَمْوَاتِ يَا جَامِعَ الشَّتَاتِ\nYAA RAADDA MAA QAD FAATA YAA NAASHIRAL AMWAATI YAA JAAMI'ASH SHATAAT\nO He Who has the power to restore that which has been missed! O He Who resurrects the dead bodies! O He Who draws together the dispersal!\nيَا رَازِقَ مَنْ يَشَاءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ\nYAA RAAZIQA MAN YASHAA'U BIGHAYRI HISAAB\nO He Who provides sustenance to whomever He wants without measure!\nوَيَا فَاعِلَ مَا يَشَاءُ كَيْفَ يَشَاءُ\nWA YAA FAA'ILA MAA YASHAA'U KAYFA YASHAA'\nO He Who has power to do whatever He wills however He wills!\nوَيَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ\nWA YAA DHAL JALAALI WAL IKRAAM\nO Lord of Majesty and Honor!\nيَا حَيُّ يَا قَيُّوْمُ يَا حَيًّا حِيْنَ لَا حَيَّ\nYAA HAYYU YAA QAYYOOMU YAA HAYYAN HEENA LAA HAYY\nO Ever-living! O Self-subsistent! O He Who existed when there existed nothing else!\nيَا حَيُّ يَا مُحْيِيَ الْمَوْتٰى يَا حَيُّ\nYAA HAYYU YAA MUHYIYAL MAWTAA YAA HAYY\nO Ever-living! O Reviver of the dead! O Ever-living!\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ بَدِيْعُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْاَرْضِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTA BADEE'US SAMAAWAATI WAL ARD\nThere is no god save You the excellent Maker of the heavens and the earth.\nيَا اِلٰهِيْ وَسَيِّدِيْ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nYAA ILAAHEE WA SAYYIDEE SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO my God and my Master, (please do) send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَارْحَمْ مُحَمَّدًا وَاٰلَ مُحَمَّدٍ\nWARHAM MUHAMMADAN WA AALA MUHAMMAD\nhave mercy upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَبَارِكْ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nWA BAARIK A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nand send benedictions upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad\nكَمَا صَلَّيْتَ وَبَارَكْتَ وَرَحِمْتَ [تَرَحَّمْتَ‏] عَلٰى اِبْرَاهِيْمَ وَاٰلِ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ\nKAMAA SALLAYTA WA BAARAKTA WA RAHIMTA [TARAHHAMTA] A'LAA IBRAAHEEMA WA AALI IBRAAHEEM\njust as You have sent blessings and benedictions and had mercy upon Abraham and the household of Abraham.\nاِنَّكَ حَمِيْدٌ مَجِيْدٌ\nINNAKA HAMEEDUN MAJEED\nYou are verily worthy of all praise and full of all glory.\nوَارْحَمْ ذُلِّي وَفَاقَتِيْ وَفَقْرِيْ وَانْفِرَادِيْ وَوَحْدَتِي\nWARHAM DHULLEE WA FAAQATEE WA FAQREE WANFIRAADEE WA WAHDATEE\nHave mercy upon my humiliation, neediness, poverty, loneliness, aloneness,\nوَخُضُوْعِيْ بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ وَاعْتِمَادِيْ عَلَيْكَ وَتَضَرُّعِيْ اِلَيْكَ\nWA KHUDOO'EE BAYNA YADAYKA WA'TIMAADEE A'LAYKA WA TADARRU'EE ILAYK\nhumbleness before You, reliance upon You, and submission to You.\nاَدْعُوْكَ دُعَاءَ الْخَاضِعِ الذَّلِيْلِ الْخَاشِعِ الْخَاۤئِفِ الْمُشْفِقِ\nAD'OOKA DU'AA'AL KHAADI'IDH DHALEELIL KHAASHI'IL KHAA'IFIL MUSHFIQ\nI implore You with the imploring of the humble, the subservient, the fearful, the scared the afraid,\nالْبَاۤئِسِ الْمَهِيْنِ الْحَقِيْرِ الْجَاۤئِعِ الْفَقِيْرِ\nAL-BAA'ISIL MAHEENIL HAQEERIL JAA'I'IL FAQEER\nthe miserable, the modest, the insignificant, the hungry, the poor,\nالْعَاۤئِذِ الْمُسْتَجِيْرِ الْمُقِرِّ بِذَنْبِهِ الْمُسْتَغْفِرِ مِنْهُ الْمُسْتَكِيْنِ لِرَبِّهٖ\nAL-A'A'IDHIL MUSTAJEERIL MUQIRRI BIDHANBIHIL MUSTAGHFIRI MINHUL MUSTAKEENI LIRABBIH\nthe seeker of Your refuge, the seeker of Your protection, the confessing of his sins, the implorer for You to forgive his sin, and the humble to his Lord;\nدُعَاءَ مَنْ اَسْلَمَتْهُ ثِقَتُهٗ [نَفْسُهٗ‏] وَرَفَضَتْهُ اَحِبَّتُهٗ وَعَظُمَتْ فَجِيْعَتُهٗ\nDU'AA'A MAN ASLAMAT-HU THIQATUHOO [NAFSUHOO] WA RAFADAT-HU AHIBBATUHOO WA A'ZUMAT FAJEE'ATUH\nI implore You with the imploration of one whom has been disappointed by those whom he trusts, rejected by his intimate ones, and whose catastrophe has been enormous.\nدُعَاءَ حَرِقٍ حَزِيْنٍ ضَعِيْفٍ مَهِيْنٍ بَاۤئِسٍ مُسْتَكِيْنٍ بِكَ مُسْتَجِيْرٍ\nDU'AA'A HARIQIN HAZEENIN DA'EEFIN MAHEENIN BAA'ISIN MUSTAKEENIN BIKA MUSTAJEER\nI implore You the imploration of one burning, sad, weak, mortified, depressed, wretched, and resorting to Your shelter.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَاَسْاَلُكَ بِاَنَّكَ مَلِيْكٌ\nALLAAHUMMA WA AS'ALUKA BI-ANNAKA MALEEK\nO Allah, I also beseech You in the name of Your being the King,\nوَاَنَّكَ مَا تَشَاءُ مِنْ اَمْرٍ يَكُوْنُ وَاَنَّكَ عَلٰى مَا تَشَاءُ قَدِيْرٌ\nWA ANNAKA MAA TASHAA'U MIN AMRIN YAKOONU WA ANNAKA A'LAA MAA TASHAA'U QADEER\nwhatever You will shall definitely take place, and You have power over all things.\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ بِحُرْمَةِ هٰذَا الشَّهْرِ الْحَرَامِ وَالْبَيْتِ الْحَرَامِ وَالْبَلَدِ الْحَرَامِ\nWA AS'ALUKA BIHURMATI HAADHASH SHAHRIL HARAAMI WAL BAYTIL HARAAMI WAL BALADIL HARAAM\nI beseech You in the name of the holiness of this sacred month, the Sacred House, the Sacred Town,\nوَالرُّكْنِ وَالْمَقَامِ وَالْمَشَاعِرِ الْعِظَامِ\nWAR RUKNI WAL MAQAAMI WAL MASHAA'IRIL I'ZAAM\nthe Rukn (i.e. the corner of the Holy Ka'bah), the Maqam (i.e. the standing-place of Prophet Abraham), the great rituals,\nوَبِحَقِّ نَبِيِّكَ مُحَمَّدٍ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ السَّلَامُ\nWA BIHAQQI NABIYYIKA MUHAMMADIN A'LAYHI WA AALIHIS SALAAM\nand in the name of Your Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him and his Household.\nيَا مَنْ وَهَبَ لِاٰدَمَ شَيْثًا، وَلِاِبْرَاهِيْمَ اِسْمَاعِيْلَ وَاِسْحَاقَ\nYAA MAN WAHABA LI-AADAMA SHAYTHAN WA LI-IBRAAHEEMA ISMAA'EELA WA IS-HAAQ\nO He Who gave Shayth to Adam, and gave Ishmael and Isaac to Abraham!\nوَيَا مَنْ رَدَّ يُوْسُفَ عَلٰى يَعْقُوْبَ\nWA YAA MAN RADDA YOOSUFA A'LAA YA'QOOB\nO He Who returned Joseph to Jacob!\nوَيَا مَنْ كَشَفَ بَعْدَ الْبَلَاءِ ضُرَّ اَيُّوْبَ\nWA YAA MAN KASHAFA BA'DAL BALAA'I DURRA AYYOOB\nO He Who relieved Job from his harm after long hardships!\nيَا رَادَّ مُوْسَىٰ عَلٰى اُمِّهٖ\nYAA RAADDA MOOSAA A'LAA UMMIH\nO He Who returned Moses to his mother!\nوَزَاۤئِدَ الْخِضْرِ فِي عِلْمِهٖ\nWA ZAA'IDAL KHIDRI FEE I'LMIH\nO He Who increased al-Khadir knowledge!\nوَيَا مَنْ وَهَبَ لِدَاوُدَ سُلَيْمَانَ وَلِزَكَرِيَّا يَحْيَىٰ وَلِمَرْيَمَ عِيْسَىٰ\nWA YAA MAN WAHABA LIDAAWUDA SULAYMAANA WA LIZAKARIYYAA YAHYAA WA LIMARYAMA I'EESAA\nO He Who gave Solomon to David, gave John to Zachariah, and gave Jesus to Mary!\nيَا حَافِظَ بِنْتِ شُعَيْبٍ\nYAA HAAFIZA BINTI SHU'AYB\nO He Who safeguarded the daughter of Shu'ayb!\nوَيَا كَافِلَ وَلَدِ اُمِّ مُوْسَىٰ\nWA YAA KAAFILA WALADI UMMI MOOSAA\nO He Who cared for the son of the mother of Moses!\nاَسْاَلُكَ اَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAS'ALUKA AN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nI beseech You to send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَاَنْ تَغْفِرَ لِي ذُنُوْبِيْ كُلَّهَا وَتُجِيْرَنِي مِنْ عَذَابِكَ\nWA AN TAGHFIRA LEE DHUNOOBEE KULLAHAA WA TUJEERANEE MIN A'DHAABIK\nforgive my all sins, save me from Your chastisement,\nوَتُوْجِبَ لِي رِضْوَانَكَ وَاَمَانَكَ وَاِحْسَانَكَ وَغُفْرَانَكَ وَجِنَانَكَ\nWA TOOJIBA LEE RIDWAANAKA WA AMAANAKA WA IHSAANAKA WA GHUFRAANAKA WA JINAANAK\nand confer upon me with Your pleasure and security and with Your favoring, forgiveness, and gardens of Your Paradise.\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ اَنْ تَفُكَّ عَنِّيْ كُلَّ حَلْقَةٍ بَيْنِيْ وَبَيْنَ مَنْ يُؤْذِيْنِيْ\nWA AS'ALUKA AN TAFUKKA A'NNEE KULLA HALQATIN BAYNEE WA BAYNA MAN YU'DHEENEE\nI ask You to redeem me from all circles of misfortune that are drawn around those who intend harm to me and me,\nوَتَفْتَحَ لِيْ كُلَّ بَابٍ وَتُلَيِّنَ لِيْ كُلَّ صَعْبٍ وَتُسَهِّلَ لِيْ كُلَّ عَسِيْرٍ\nWA TAFTAHA LEE KULLA BAABIN WA TULAYYINA LEE KULLA SA'BIN WA TUSAHHILA LEE KULLA A'SEER\nunlock for me all doors, make easy for me all hardships, alleviate for me all difficult matters,\nوَتُخْرِسَ عَنِّيْ كُلَّ نَاطِقٍ بِشَرٍّ وَتَكُفَّ عَنِّيْ كُلَّ بَاغٍ\nWA TUKHRISA A'NNEE KULLA NAATIQIN BISHARRIN WA TAKUFFA A'NNEE KULLA BAAGH\nmute all those who speak ill of me, defend me against all oppressors,\nوَتَكْبِتَ [عَنِّي‏] كُلَّ عَدُوٍّ لِيْ وَحَاسِدٍ وَتَمْنَعَ مِنِّيْ كُلَّ ظَالِمٍ\nWA TAKBITA [A'NNEE] KULLA A'DUWWIN LEE WA HAASIDIN WA TAMNA'A MINNEE KULLA ZAALIM\nsuppress all my enemies and envious ones, protect me against all unjust ones,\nوَتَكْفِيَنِيْ كُلَّ عَاۤئِقٍ يَحُوْلُ بَيْنِيْ وَبَيْنَ حَاجَتِيْ\nWA TAKFIYANEE KULLA A'A'IQIN YAHOOLU BAYNEE WA BAYNA HAAJATEE\nand rescue me from all impediments that lie between my needs and me,\nوَيُحَاوِلُ اَنْ يُفَرِّقَ بَيْنِيْ وَبَيْنَ طَاعَتِكَ وَيُثَبِّطَنِيْ عَنْ عِبَادَتِكَ\nWA YUHAAWILU AN YUFARRIQA BAYNEE WA BAYNA TAA'ATIKA WA YUTHABBITANEE A'N I'BAADATIK\ntry to take me away from acts of obedience to You, and try to frustrate me from serving You.\nيَا مَنْ اَلْجَمَ الْجِنَّ الْمُتَمَرِّدِيْنَ وَقَهَرَ عُتَاةَ الشَّيَاطِيْنِ\nYAA MAN ALJAMAL JINNAL MUTAMARRIDEENA WA QAHARA U'TAATASH SHAYAATEEN\nO He Who has bridled all mutinous jinn, overcome all tyrannical devils,\nوَاَذَلَّ رِقَابَ الْمُتَجَبِّرِيْنَ وَرَدَّ كَيْدَ الْمُتَسَلِّطِيْنَ عَنِ الْمُسْتَضْعَفِيْنَ\nWA ADHALLA RIQAABAL MUTAJABBIREENA WA RADDA KAYDAL MUTASALLITEENA A'NIL MUSTAD'AFEEN\nmortified the necks of the oppressors, and deterred all the ruling authorities from harming the enfeebled ones!\nاَسْاَلُكَ بِقُدْرَتِكَ عَلٰى مَا تَشَاءُ وَتَسْهِيْلِكَ لِمَا تَشَاءُ كَيْفَ تَشَاءُ\nAS'ALUKA BIQUDRATIKA A'LAA MAA TASHAA'U WA TAS-HEELIKA LIMAA TASHAA'U KAYFA TASHAA'\nI beseech You in the name of Your power over all things and Your alleviating whatever You will however You will,\nاَنْ تَجْعَلَ قَضَاءَ حَاجَتِيْ فِيْمَا تَشَاءُ\nAN TAJ'ALA QADAA'A HAAJATEE FEEMAA TASHAA'\nto grant my requests as You will.\nThen prostrate, pressing your cheeks to the ground, and recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَكَ سَجَدْتُ وَبِكَ اٰمَنْتُ\nALLAAHUMMA LAKA SAJADTU WA BIKA AAMANT\nO Allah, I am prostrating myself before You and I have full faith in You;\nفَارْحَمْ ذُلِّي وَفَاقَتِيْ وَاجْتِهَادِيْ وَتَضَرُّعِيْ وَمَسْكَنَتِيْ وَفَقْرِيْ اِلَيْكَ يَا رَبِّ\nFARHAM DHULLEE WA FAAQATEE WAJTIHAADEE WA TADARRU'EE WA MASKANATEE WA FAQREE ILAYKA YAA RABB\nso, (please) have mercy upon my humility, neediness, efforts, meekness, paucity, and my want to You, O my Lord.\nTry to shed at least a single tear, for this is the sign that the dua is accepted.",
  "merits": "The most important rite on the fifteenth of Rajab is the supplicatory prayer known as Dua Umm Dawud. This great supplicatory prayer brings about innumerable rewards some of which are that it grants the requests, relieves from anguishes, and saves from the persecutions of the wrongdoers.\n\nShaykh al-Tusi describes the rite in his book Misbah al-Mutahajjid."
}
